title: 'statement-store: disconnect a peer that reads statements too slowly'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A peer is now disconnected, with no reputation change, when its last two statement sends
    failed or its propagation outbox overflowed behind a chunk in flight. Its reconnect gets a
    fresh initial sync. Before, such a peer kept its connection and lost statements.

    A full outbox refuses new hashes instead of dropping its oldest. Disconnects are counted in
    `substrate_sync_statement_stalled_peers_disconnected`.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
